 `aidlc/spaces/<space>/checkers.json` and shows what it recorded. Edit the file
 by hand afterwards as you like; other hosts read the same file.
 
+### Prewalk on the developer
+
+`aidlc-developer-agent` also carries `prewalk: true`. The developer starts on
+its normal model, reads the approved plan and records its steps with `todo`.
+At its first edit or write after that, Coding Harness hands the rest of the
+implementation to the `smol` model role. Assign that role (`modelRoles.smol`),
+because an unassigned `smol` inherits the default model and the handoff becomes
+a no-op. Override per agent with the harness's own `task.agentPrewalk` setting
+(`off`, `on` or a model pattern for `aidlc-developer-agent`, also under
+`/agents`). For the conductor itself, use the harness's session-level
+`prewalk.enabled`.
+
 ## Alongside Claude Code
 
 One project can carry both distributions: run `aidlc config --harness claude`
